<h2 id="ha-ctrl-010-acceptance">Acceptance checks</h2>

1. Check the exact start and end times, touching blocks, an overlap that is rejected and an overnight pair across two days. Confirm the linked automation sees no invented off and on change.
2. Test an all-day event, a timed event, a read-only calendar and an unavailable calendar. Keep the provider's limits on repeating events.
3. Check the installation zone, a different viewer zone, the hour that is skipped in spring and the hour that repeats in autumn. Record what Home Assistant actually does.
4. Pause and resume a timer, then restart with restore on and off in a test setup. Check that a missed finish is explained and that edit, save and cancel work by keyboard.

Source review and these checks do not prove an accessible result on a real device. Record the versions, input, expected and observed results and where the evidence is kept.

